From 3b395507c60408b84b71f4badd66b4b89e0ab0b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mukayi <1515982581@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:57:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] fix(metrics): take the step's batch on the worker
 thread

report_step took the batch before awaiting asyncio.to_thread. If Serve
cancelled the request (client disconnect) while the job was still queued,
the job never ran, CancelledError skipped the restore, and the batch was
lost. Restoring on cancellation instead would repeat the batch whenever
the job had already started.

Take, report and restore now all happen in _report_buffered_step on the
worker thread: a cancelled queued job leaves the batch buffered, and a
running job reports it exactly once.

(cherry picked from commit e4bd440761f2a0ed88906bc63c87cd9a8f636427)
---
 relax/utils/metrics/service.py               | 47 +++++++++---------
 tests/utils/test_metrics_client_transport.py | 52 +++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 71 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

